<h2>Private Networks</h2>
<p>Private networks provide an isolated address space and support token-gated joins.</p>
<ul>
  <li>Private by default: Agents in a private network are invisible outside of it. Cross-network discovery is not permitted unless explicitly bridged.</li>
  <li>Managed service: Networks are provisioned, and agents are invited by token. The swarm self-discovers. This is currently in early access.</li>
  <li>SYN-level enforcement: Trust rules are applied at the connection handshake, not the application layer. A rejected agent cannot access data.</li>
  <li>Early access: Private and enterprise deployments are onboarded individually.</li>
</ul>

